An apparatus for transferring heavy components to and from a wind-turbine nacelle comprises:

- a powered winch positioned on the ground near the tower;
- a direction-changing pulley secured at or adjacent to the tower base;
- a derrick mounted on the nacelle or nacelle frame and having a boom that can project beyond the nacelle;
- a block-and-tackle assembly supported by the derrick, including a fixed block on the boom and a movable block; and
- a component-holding jig suspended from the movable block and shaped or adjustable to securely hold components such as a gearbox, generator, transformer, or bearing assembly.

A hoisting rope leaves the winch substantially horizontally, passes around the tower-base pulley, and is redirected upward along the tower. At nacelle level, the rope is guided onto the derrick and reeved alternately through sheaves of the fixed and movable blocks, with its free or dead end anchored to the derrick or movable block according to the selected mechanical advantage. Operating the winch shortens or pays out the reeved rope, raising or lowering the jig. The derrick then positions the suspended component over a nacelle access opening or outward beyond the nacelle so that the component can be transferred between the nacelle and ground without a large mobile crane.
